		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνεκ-πλώω</span></b> : fut.
		inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πλευσεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					13.25
				</span></i>
			:—<i>sail out along with</i>, c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.5
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετά τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					13.27
				</span></i>
			: abs., ib.<i><span class="en">
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.3
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Συνεκπλέουσα</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αι</span>, name of a Comedy by
		Philippides.</div>
